  "fab_notes": [
    "1. Material: FR-4, 1.6 mm, 6 layers, JLCPCB JLC06161H-3313 stackup (sheet 2 table).",
    "2. Copper: 1 oz outer, 0.5 oz inner. Surface finish: lead-free HASL.",
    "3. Solder mask green, silkscreen white, both sides. Vias tented.",
    "4. Fabricate to IPC-6012 Class 2. Electrical test 100 %.",
    "5. Dimensions in mm. Tolerances unless noted: outline ±0.2, finished holes ±0.08.",
    "6. Fabricate from the Gerber and drill files of the same revision as this drawing.",
    "7. Minimum trace width 0.20 mm. Smallest hole Ø0.30 (vias) on Ø0.61 pads: 0.15 mm annular ring.",
    "8. The 4 plated mounting holes are not connected to any net; keep them isolated on all layers.",
    "9. No slots, controlled impedance, castellations, edge plating or gold fingers."
  ],
  "bom_notes": [
    "1. INSTALLED BY: JLCPCB = fitted by the JLCPCB assemblers (SMT and through-hole) before delivery; After delivery = fitted by the builder.",
    "2. PROCESS gives the assembly process and the side the part is on.",
    "3. The Teensy 4.1 (on H1 / H2) and the display (on H3) are fitted at module level, see KC-01-1910. P5 / P6 take the DFPlayer Mini audio module; SPKR1 / SPKR2 the speakers.",
    "4. Substitutes need the approval of the design authority."
  ],
  "assembler": "JLCPCB",
  "after_delivery": [],
  "place_polarised": [
    "D1",
    "LED1",
    "C12"
  ],
  "place_label_size": 1.0,
  "place_notes": [
    "1. All parts are on the bottom side except the display header H3, which is on the top side.",
    "2. The bottom view is drawn as seen holding the board bottom side up (flipped left to right), so the datum is at the top right.",
    "3. Red dot = pin 1 of every part with more than two pins, the cathode of D1, the anode of LED1 and the + terminal of C12. These match the silkscreen marks.",
    "4. U3 (safe switch): 1 SW_P = +5V, 2 / 3 / 5 V_EN, 4 GND, 6 input to INT_SAFE; wired as on the Panel Hub.",
    "5. Part centres, rotations and part numbers are in the placement table (last sheet), measured from the datum (top view)."
  ],
